# EXAMPLE 3: Agents on DIFFERENT providers in the same graph
#
# Each agent has EXACTLY one model, but the graph mixes providers freely:
#   researcher -> gemini  (fast and cheap for search/summarization)
#   architect  -> claude  (complex reasoning)
#   coder      -> gpt-4o  (code generation)
#   reviewer   -> claude  (careful checking)
#
# Agents are added with the explicit provider:
#   pixelgo agent add ai <ws> researcher gemini    gemini-2.0-flash "You are a researcher." "read_file,list_dir"
#   pixelgo agent add ai <ws> architect  anthropic claude-sonnet-5  "You are an architect." "read_file"
#   pixelgo agent add ai <ws> coder      openai    gpt-4o           "You are a programmer."  "read_file,write_file"
#   pixelgo agent add ai <ws> reviewer   anthropic claude-sonnet-5  "You are a reviewer."    "read_file"

entry researcher

node researcher
node architect
node coder
node reviewer

edge researcher -> architect
edge architect  -> coder
edge coder      -> reviewer

edge reviewer -> coder when NEEDS_FIX
edge reviewer -> END   when APPROVED
